# M24.4 item 3 prep -- first-ever attempt to boot the M24.3 cFS artifact
# (third_party/cfs/build-rtems_zynqmp/exe/cpu1/core-cpu1.exe) under Renode. M24.3's own report
# states explicitly: "The RTEMS binary has never been executed." This script is that first
# attempt, against our own fixed platform file (item 1) -- BSP_RESET_BOARD_AT_EXIT is NOT yet
# fixed in THIS specific binary (it was only rebuilt into the isolated
# rtems-bsp-noreset/myout prefix for the ticker/hello samples, item 2's own "what is NOT yet
# done" note) -- so a clean exit from this binary, if it ever reaches one, would still spin;
# this smoke test is about whether cFE/OSAL/the lockstep apps boot at all, not about exit
# behavior.
#
# UART0 is cFE's own debug console (question 148/M24.3: this BSP's two Zynq UARTs are
# ttyS0=UART0 debug console, ttyS1=UART1 the lockstep transport). No backend is attached to
# uart1 in this smoke test (no bridge yet) -- io_lockstep's open()/read()/write() on
# /dev/ttyS1 should still succeed against the bare peripheral model even with nothing
# listening on the other end; whether the app *blocks* waiting for a HELLO that never arrives
# is exactly one of the things this smoke test is watching for.

:name: av-m24-4-cfs-boot-smoke

using sysbus
using sysbus.cluster0
using sysbus.cluster1

mach create "av-m24-4-cfs-boot-smoke"

machine LoadPlatformDescription @/Users/probe/code/AltaVista/third_party/renode/platforms/cpus/zynqmp.repl

uart0 CreateFileBackend $ORIGIN/cfs_boot_uart0.log true

macro reset
"""
    cluster0 ForEach IsHalted true
    cluster1 ForEach IsHalted true
    rpu0 IsHalted false

    sysbus LoadELF @/Users/probe/code/AltaVista/third_party/cfs/build-rtems_zynqmp/exe/cpu1/core-cpu1.exe cpu=rpu0
"""

runMacro $reset
